# TeamWeave - Hackathon Team Matcher Portal

A specialized recruitment and team-building portal designed for hackathons and large-scale academic projects. Participants input their technical proficiencies and project interests, while organizers can monitor the talent pool and automatically suggest balanced, cross-functional teams.

## 📋 Project Overview

TeamWeave solves the challenge of manual team formation by using intelligent clustering algorithms to automatically group participants into balanced teams that ensure complementary skills (frontend, backend, data, design, etc.) rather than skill overlap.

## 🚀 Features

### 1. Participant Profile & Skill Input
- Self-registration with name, email, and technical skills
- Proficiency level tracking (1-5 scale)
- Project interests tracking
- Profile status management

### 2. Skill Management
- Pre-configured skill categories:
  - **Frontend**: React, Vue.js, Angular, HTML/CSS, JavaScript
  - **Backend**: C#, Python, Java, Node.js, PHP
  - **Data**: SQL, Machine Learning, Data Analysis, Big Data
  - **Design**: UI/UX Design, Graphic Design, Figma, Web Design
  - **DevOps**: Docker, Kubernetes, AWS, Azure, CI/CD

### 3. Intelligent Clustering Algorithm
- **K-means clustering** on skill vectors for initial grouping
- **Constraint-based balancing** to ensure skill diversity
- Euclidean distance and cosine similarity calculations
- Automatic team size adjustment based on participant pool

### 4. Team Management
- Create and organize teams with automatic or manual assignment
- Move participants between teams (with constraint checking)
- Lock teams to prevent further modifications
- Individual participant locking flags

### 5. Organizer Dashboard
- Monitor full talent pool in real-time
- Filter by skill category
- Export participant and team data to CSV
- View team composition and coverage

### 6. Audit Trail & Compliance
- Complete audit logging of all team changes
- Track who made changes, what changed, and when
- Manual adjustment history
- Actor attribution (Organizer/System)

## 🏗️ Architecture

### Core Components

```
Models/
├── Participant.cs          # Participant entity with skills & interests
├── Skill.cs               # Skill definitions with categories
├── ParticipantSkill.cs    # Join table with proficiency levels
├── Team.cs                # Team entity
├── TeamMember.cs          # Team membership join table
├── ClusteringRun.cs       # Clustering execution record
└── AuditLog.cs            # Change tracking

Services/
├── ParticipantService.cs      # Participant registration & management
├── TeamService.cs             # Team operations & auditing
├── ClusteringService.cs       # K-means & balancing algorithms
└── SkillVectorEncoder.cs      # Vector math & similarity calculations

Utilities/
├── SkillRepository.cs     # Pre-configured skill catalog
└── DataExporter.cs        # CSV export functionality
```

### Algorithm Details

**Skill Vector Encoding**
- Each participant's skills are encoded as a vector
- Proficiency levels normalized to 0-1 range
- Skill index maps skill names to vector dimensions

**K-means Clustering**
- Initializes centroids with random participants
- Iteratively assigns participants to nearest cluster
- Recalculates centroids based on cluster members
- Converges when centroid movement falls below threshold

**Team Balancing**
- Calculates skill diversity score per participant
- Greedily selects participants ensuring skill category coverage
- Verifies each team has required skill categories
- Falls back to constraint relaxation if needed

## 📊 Data Models

### Participant
- `Id`: Unique identifier
- `Name`: Participant name (required)
- `Email`: Email address (required)
- `ProfileStatus`: Registration status
- `Skills`: Collection of proficiency-tagged skills
- `Interests`: Project interests
- `Teams`: Team assignments

### Team
- `Id`: Unique identifier
- `Name`: Team name
- `EventId`: Associated event
- `Status`: Draft/Suggested/Locked/Finalized
- `IsLocked`: Prevents auto-matching changes
- `Members`: Participant list

### Skill
- `Id`: Unique identifier
- `Name`: Skill name
- `Category`: Skill classification
- `ParticipantSkills`: Usage references

## 🎯 Usage Example

```csharp
// 1. Initialize services
var participantService = new ParticipantService();
var teamService = new TeamService();
var clusteringService = new ClusteringService();

// 2. Register participants
var alice = participantService.RegisterParticipant(
    "Alice", "alice@example.com", new List<string> { "React" }
);
participantService.AddSkillToParticipant(
    alice.Id, SkillRepository.GetSkillByName("React"), 5
);

// 3. Run clustering
var teams = clusteringService.ClusterParticipants(participants, teamSize: 4);

// 4. Create teams
foreach (var cluster in teams)
{
    var team = teamService.CreateTeam($"Team {i++}", eventId: 1);
    foreach (var participant in cluster)
    {
        teamService.AddParticipantToTeam(team.Id, participant);
    }
}

// 5. Manage teams
teamService.MoveParticipantBetweenTeams(participantId, fromTeamId, toTeamId);
teamService.LockTeam(teamId, "Organizer");

// 6. Audit
var logs = teamService.GetAuditLogs();
```

## 📈 Performance Specifications

- **Clustering**: Up to 1,000 participants in under 30 seconds
- **Team Size**: Configurable (typically 3-6 members)
- **Scalability**: Supports concurrent events with isolated participant pools
- **Memory**: Efficient vector operations with minimal allocation

## 🔒 Security & Privacy

- PII (email, contact info) handled securely
- Role-based access controls (Participant vs. Organizer)
- Audit trail for compliance
- Event-level data isolation

